<title>BELGIUM: GBL H1 1996 group net profit up 12 pct.</title>
<headline>GBL H1 1996 group net profit up 12 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>First-half 1996 earnings</p>
<p>(billion Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net (excludes minorities)     4.46 vs     3.98</p>
<p>    Group earnings/share (francs)     190    vs   169</p>
<p>NOTE - Groupe Bruxelles Lambert SA (GBL) is Belgium's second-biggest holding company.  </p>
<p>Group share in companies consolidated by equity method</p>
<p>						    3.96 vs     3.59</p>
<p>    Dividends				   0.27 vs     0.08</p>
<p>    Net financial income		    0.38 vs     0.17</p>
<p>    Cons current profit		     4.51 vs     3.74</p>
<p>    Capital gains, extraord. gains	0.26 vs     0.51</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
